{"caption":"Inside a microgravity module, a man with short gray hair, glasses, a green polo shirt, tan trousers and a black wristwatch floats in the left foreground, viewed from behind. He extends his right hand and balances a small metallic dome-shaped object on the tip of his index finger. The white paneled wall behind him is crossed by a thin diagonal cable and a horizontal dark cable, with two circular hatch covers at the top, a fabric bag on the right and a blue rail along the bottom.

Across the bulk of the excerpt the metallic object remains resting on the fingertip with essentially no change in position relative to the hand or the panel. The man's head, arm and body hold their orientation, and only tiny successive vertical differences hint at slow floating drift. The diagonal and horizontal cables, the hatch covers and the bag keep identical positions throughout, confirming the camera is stationary and the apparent stillness belongs to the balanced object.

Toward the close of the excerpt the object shifts and blurs. It displaces horizontally from the fingertip. A motion-blur streak trails across the panel as it starts to drift away.","length_note":""}
